WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00.650 --> 00:10.370
Aaliyah asked Noah to identify which new ideas developed by his team are the most effective for MODA to invest in as a part of this transformation.

2
00:11.010 --> 00:19.910
So Noah reaches out to Maryam, who can help him gather and analyse information from across the Digital team on their top three ideas.

3
00:20.330 --> 00:28.100
Maryam has spent the last week talking to different members of Noah’s team to gather the reasons why these ideas are the best to pursue.

4
00:29.190 --> 00:34.660
There was a ton of information to work with, but she now feels confident to share her findings with Noah.

5
00:35.530 --> 00:41.250
“And the second idea is a very good idea from Penelope, which proposes in-store self-serve tablets.

6
00:41.250 --> 00:46.449
I can walk you through the report on the estimated costs and benefits.” “Okay, but first…”

7
00:46.449 --> 00:51.360
“That reminds me that Harry also shared how his idea builds on Penelope’s idea, and…”

8
00:51.780 --> 00:56.320
“You want this. It shows how everything can integrate with a new point-of-sale system.”

9
00:56.650 --> 00:57.540
“Maryam…” “And?”

10
00:58.090 --> 01:03.430
“One last thing on the third idea — super important given the recent advances in technology.

11
01:03.850 --> 01:11.910
We can negotiate an extremely favourable price with our vendor and save money in the long term. Oh, before I forget…” “Maryam.”

12
01:12.520 --> 01:14.270
“Maryam!” “I’m out.”

13
01:15.140 --> 01:18.950
“I’m sorry to cut you off. This is all really interesting indeed.

14
01:19.460 --> 01:23.360
But have we answered yet why these are the best ideas to pursue?”

15
01:24.200 --> 01:30.180
“Oh. I wanted to share all of the findings from the team first. They did so much work.”

16
01:30.980 --> 01:35.200
“It’s really great work. You definitely have all the right pieces.

17
01:35.810 --> 01:39.140
You just need to find a way to communicate it in a clearer way.

18
01:39.850 --> 01:44.350
How about we structure the information you have received so far?” “Okay.” “In our meeting with Aaliyah,

19
01:46.600 --> 01:53.350
we want to lead with the answer — the governing thought — and then provide the reasoning and facts to support it.

20
01:54.250 --> 01:58.210
Here’s what I had in mind. Let’s use this as a starting point.”

21
01:58.980 --> 02:05.730
“Right.” “Now, this key message will raise a new question in the reader’s mind, such as “why?” or “how?”.

22
02:06.600 --> 02:15.140
To answer that question, we need to go down to the next level — or key line — to answer why these three ideas are the best to invest in.

23
02:15.650 --> 02:20.130
That will prompt another question, which we can answer with the supporting facts.

24
02:20.740 --> 02:24.390
Let’s group the information you’ve collected and see what themes emerge.

25
02:25.030 --> 02:31.810
Then we can figure out why each group of facts really matters — what people refer to as the “so what”.” “Got it.”

